  "result": "I wrote the revised record for NRS_484B_260 to `record.jsonl`. Nothing has been run against the gate yet.\n\n**What failed:** the `blind` scenario hid `rel.bearing`. Hiding it only removes the measured bearing. The rule then works the bearing out from the other vehicle's position and heading and the subject's position. A track can't be admitted without those, so `rel.bearing` could never make the verdict unknown.\n\n**What changed:** only `blind`. It now hides `st.on_way` instead. That is a map relation the source records; Core never computes it from motion.\n- **Applicability:** whether roadway r lies on highway h becomes unknown.\n- **Obligation:** whether the other vehicle's lane lies on that same highway becomes unknown.\n- Everything else in the scene stays as in `forbid`: the subject straddles the entrance and the roadway, and the closest approach is still a conflict. So the only thing that can make the verdict unknown is the hidden atom.\n\nEverything else in the record is as before. That includes the `rel.bearing` reading of \"approaching\" in s6, which is still a fair reading of the law.\n\n**Risk:** I'm assuming hiding `st.on_way` blanks the `ways` field the witness builders set; I have no Core source in hand to confirm it. If Core doesn't blank it, `blind` will fail the gate again and needs a different hidden atom.\n\nThe coder needs to rebuild the `blind` witness as the `forbid` scene with `st.on_way` hidden. The current witness file still has `blind` as a copy of `forbid` with `rel.bearing` hidden.",
